l\",\"read_scope\":\"定向阅读上述定义与例子，2026-10-24。\",\"title\":\"Building Topology Ontology (BOT) specification\",\"url\":\"https://w3c-lbd-cg.github.io/bot/\"},{\"can_support\":\"After plan lines, room polygons, openings, and a scale-aware coordinate system have been traced, calculate 2D lengths/areas/distances and candidate contains/intersects/touches relations reproducibly.\",\"cannot_support\":\"It does not extract or semantically recognize a drawing, establish that traced coordinates match a real building, or calculate roof slope from z; z is ignored in its geometric analysis.\",\"claim\":\"For coordinate-defined planar geometries, Shapely provides deterministic area, length, distance, and topological predicates. It explicitly performs analysis in the x-y plane and ignores z.\",\"locator\":\"Geometric objects and coordinate systems; General Attributes and Methods (area, length, distance); predicates intersects, touches, within.\",\"read_scope\":\"Read the coordinate-system and geometry notes, measurement methods, and topological-predicate sections; not the full manual.\",\"title\":\"The Shapely User Manual\",\"url\":\"https://shapely.readthedocs.io/en/stable/manual.html\"},{\"can_support\":\"A plan-derived topology baseline for room boundaries, wall incidence, adjacency, and connectivity, once linework is available.\",\"cannot_support\":\"Automatic interpretation of untraced drawings, reliable semantic/material classification without annotation, or transfer of the reported algorithm's validity to Jingning dwellings.\",\"claim\":\"The paper constructs room polygons and adjacency/connectivity/inclusion relations from building-plan linework using graph and disjoint-set methods, and reports tests on real and simulated plans. Its conclusion says semantic extraction from plan annotations is outside the method's current treatment.\",\"locator\":\"Sections 3.2 (space-wall and room-room topology), 4.3 (polygon extraction), 4.5 (complexity), 5.1-5.3 (tests), and conclusion.\",\"read_scope\":\"Read indexed full-text excerpts for the specified methods, tests, and conclusion. The publisher page was throttled, so this was not a full-paper read.\",\"title\":\"Navigation-Oriented Topological Model Construction Algorithm for Complex Indoor Space\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2220-9964/12/6/248\"},{\"can_support\":\"Run graph rules, fixed/variable-length path queries, relationship integrity checks, and grouped counts/statistics; store coordinates/derived quantities and compute supported point-to-point distances.\",\"cannot_support\":\"Without custom functions or a separate geometry engine, Cypher is not a drawing interpreter or general wall/polygon/solid geometry engine; graph paths alone do not calculate polygon area, shared-boundary length, or roof slope.\",\"claim\":\"Cypher MATCH expresses graph-pattern and path queries; count/avg/sum aggregate matched values; built-in spatial geometry is POINT (2D or 3D), with point distance requiring compatible CRS and dimensions. Spatial functions specify points and calculate point-to-point distance.\",\"locator\":\"Patterns and path matching: https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/patterns/ ; aggregating functions: https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/25/functions/aggregating/ ; spatial values and functions: https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/values-and-types/spatial/ and https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/functions/spatial/ .\",\"read_scope\":\"Read current pattern, spatial-value, and spatial-function pages; the official aggregation page was reviewed via its indexed excerpt for grouping and aggregate functions, not fully opened.\",\"title\":\"Neo4j Cypher Manual (current)\",\"url\":\"https://neo4j.com/docs/cypher-manual/current/patterns/\"},{\"can_support\":\"Use an LLM to propose/rank missing relation or label candidates, and evaluate predictions against deliberately hidden known triples in a controlled graph.\",\"cannot_support\":\"A predicted material or construction relation is not verified merely because it is plausible, well-ranked, or supported by an LLM explanation; the paper does not validate claims against architectural drawings, field measurements, or Jingning evidence.\",\"claim\":\"The paper treats completion as predicting and ranking a missing entity in an incomplete triple, combining a KG retriever with LLM re-ranking and demonstrations. It evaluates against held-out benchmark triples; this is predictive evaluation, not evidence verification for a particular building.\",\"locator\":\"Sections 1 and 3.1-3.3 define link prediction and candidate ranking; sections 4.1-4.2 describe benchmark data and MRR/Hits metrics; conclusion and limitations.\",\"read_scope\":\"Read the abstract, problem definition, method, benchmark setup, metrics/results, and limitations; not a broader KGC survey.\",\"title\":\"KICGPT: Large Language Model with Knowledge in Context for Knowledge Graph Completion\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.findings-emnlp.580/\"},{\"can_support\":\"An explicit visibility boundary for external UAV oblique imagery and a rationale for independent reference dimensions and separate indoor capture.\",\"cannot_support\":\"Internal room geometry, hidden joints/structure, material composition, or historical attributes from external imagery alone; its one-building accuracy figures are not guaranteed for another survey.\",\"claim\":\"In its single-building study, the UAV photogrammetry model represented geometry visible from outside and could not represent elements or structures not externally visible. Interior elements required a separate BIM model informed by plans and direct measurements. The study also recommends reference checks because individual take-offs could have material error even when an aggregate result looked accurate.\",\"locator\":\"Methods §§2.1-2.3; results and discussion §§3-4; conclusions §5.\",\"read_scope\":\"Read the abstract, UAV/model methods, model-comparison and take-off results, discussion, and conclusions.\",\"title\":\"Photogrammetry-based approach for collecting and processing information about an existing building\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.24425/bpasts.2023.144453\"}],\"modelBoundary\":{\"completeness\":\"只对本轮墙柱屋顶、空间、开口与基础量测任务提供可互核资料；梁架、榫卯、厨房与生活设施未展开，不能称完整实物复原。\",\"interfaceScope\":\"界面保持原身份与局部几何；INTERFACE_OF统一两侧空间及开口宿主，角色分开；BOUNDARY_PARTICIPANT记录空间边界参与，不冒称BOT邻接等价。I08—I10另一侧仍未知；不扩展为完整通行网络。\",\"materialAnalysis\":\"材料标签统一字典；同一对象可多标签。计数须先限定对象类别和层级，含某材料不等于面积、体积或质量比例。\",\"neo4jMapping\":\"统一V01主源已具备LPG编译、限定迁移与读回流程；实际是否入库以Neo4j/统一核验.json为准。不是完整BOT/OWL实现。\",\"spaceGeometry\":\"仅有平面区域及地坪标高，没有宣称封闭、无缝的三维空间实体。门洞沿墙中心线记录；与房间净边界之间有墙厚，不能直接拿平面线条相触判定通行。\"},\"modelVersion\":\"V01-unified-2.1\",\"nodes\":[{\"class\":\"Building\",\"evidence\":[\"EV01\",\"EV02\",\"EV03\",\"EV04\",\"EV05\",\"EV06\",\"EV07\",\"EV08\"],\"geometry\":{\"kind\":\"box\",\"max\":[9.6,7.2,5.6],\"min\":[0,0,0]},\"id\":\"B01\",\"labels\":[\"Building\",\"Zone\"],\"name\":\"V01虚拟主屋\",\"properties\":{\"analysisItems\":[\"D01-T01\",\"D01-T02\",\"D01-T05\",\"D04-T01\",\"D04-T02\",\"D04-T03\",\"D04-T04\",\"D04-T05\",\"D04-T06\",\"D05-T01\",\"D05-T02\",\"D05-T03\",\"D05-T04\",\"D05-T05\",\"D05-T06\",\"D06-T01\",\"D06-T02\",\"D06-T03\",\"D06-T04\",\"D06-T05\"],\"axisDepthM\":7.2,\"axisFootprintAreaM2\":69.12,\"axisWidthM\":9.6,\"caseId\":\"V01\",\"coordinateFrame\":\"V01-local-XYZ\",\"depthDirection\":\"+Y\",\"depthM\":7.2,\"eavePointXYZ\":[4.8,-0.6,3.2666666666666666],\"eaveZM\":3.2666666666666666,\"facingAzimuthDeg\":180,\"footprintShape\":\"axis-reference-rectangle\",\"footprintXY\":[0.0,0.0,9.6,0.0,9.6,7.2,0.0,7.2],\"geometryActive\":true,\"geometryVersion\":\"V01-unified-2.1\",\"groundPointXYZ\":[4.8,0.0,0.0],\"groundZM\":0.0,\"heightBasis\":\"RF01.geometry.eaveZ为挑檐外缘标高；wallSupportHeightM为墙轴承托参考，不可替代\",\"measurementBoundaryBasis\":\"主屋既有轴网矩形9.6×7.2m；非主体外墙外边线，不含挑檐\",\"precisionMeaning\":\"精确合成参数及算术，不是测绘精度\",\"recordStatus\":\"synthetic_assignment\",\"ridgeHeightM\":5.6,\"ridgePointXYZ\":[4.8,3